# madcide keybinding profile: Emacs-style — the same action vocabulary
# as joe.keys respelled onto Emacs's CONTROL chords (C-x families
# included; the chord grammar is the same data joe's ^K uses).
#
# Meta is `alt+` and C-SPC is `ctrl+space` (plan §41.11a step 3e). The
# window and the browser send Meta, as does a terminal — by reporting
# modified keys, or as the ESC prefix (ESC and the key in one burst reads
# as Alt and the key); a lone esc keeps closing panes and prompts.
# C-SPC is a terminal's NUL, so it reaches every client. The region is
# mark..caret live (no `bend` in this set), which IS the Emacs region
# model; Shift with a motion selects too (Emacs's shift-select-mode).
#
# File and exit
# The style's name in Tools ▸ Key bindings… (plan §41.11a step 3e).
@title Emacs

^x ^s save
^x ^c quit
^x ^f editfile
^x b editfile
# Buffers/project: C-x C-b (list-buffers) raises the project window.
^x ^b project
# Search
^s find
# Editing
^k delline
^d del
^_ undo
# The region and the kill ring: C-SPC sets the mark, C-w kills the region,
# M-w copies it, C-y yanks it back, C-x h marks the whole buffer.
ctrl+space mark
^w cut
alt+w copy
^y paste
^x h selectall
# Movement
^a home
^e end
^v pgdn
alt+v pgup
alt+f wordright
alt+b wordleft
alt+< top
alt+> bottom
alt+g g gotoline
# Repaint (C-l recenter's closest seat)
^l refresh
# Windows: C-x 2 / 1 / 0 / o — the direct Emacs seats.
^x 2 splitw
^x 1 onlywin
^x 0 killwin
^x o nextw
# F5 runs the buffer into the REPL tab's session: a fresh one, its main
# run, its names left for the prompt (plan §41.10a).
f5 replrun
# The project window's keys (@project scope — profile data; the baked
# defaults add esc/backspace).
@project ins projadd
@project del projdel
@project enter projopen
